\details{
\subsection{The CAR}{

Every stratum of the raised catch is a row: the landings, the discards that were
reported and the discards the raising made, whichever of the origin and the variable
the raising was run for. \code{imported} says which: \code{"N"} for the discards the raising
made (\code{importedOrRaised == "raised"}), \code{"Y"} for all the others. The two names of the
group say how the strata took part in the raising:
\itemize{
\item \code{catchAllocationGroupNameTarget}: the group the stratum was \strong{raised for}, on the
discards the raising made (\code{imported = "N"}) and on those only. It is the group of
\code{condition_raising_st_list} the stratum falls in.
\item \code{catchAllocationGroupNameSource}: the group(s) the stratum \strong{feeds}, on the donor
strata (\code{imported = "Y"}) and on those only - the landings and the discards of the
strata whose discard ratio went into a group's. A stratum that feeds several groups
has them all, separated by \code{"; "}. A group's donors are the strata of its
\code{condition_matched_data_list} condition that have a discard estimate (and landings),
and the other rows of the same domain, as \code{\link[=catchRaising]{catchRaising()}} picks them.
\item \code{catchAllocationSchemeName} is written on the raised discards only.
}

A group that raised nothing (it had no landings without an estimate, or no donor to
take a ratio from) is neither a target nor a source: it is not in the tables. A raised
discard with no total - the ratio of a group with no donor is \code{NaN} - is not a result
and is left out, with a warning.

The other fields are the catch's: \code{total} is added up for the strata that are one row
of the CAR (the format has no \code{metier6}, so a stratum the CEF splits further is added
up), and so are the counts of the sampling - \code{PSU}, \code{numPSUs} and \code{numTrips}, \code{NA} for
the raised discards, which have no sample of their own - as in \code{\link[=catchCombined]{catchCombined()}}, whose
totals the CAR adds up to. The format asks for them on every imported discard (and BMS)
stratum, and a stratum without them is counted in a warning. \code{variance} is left empty.
\code{vesselFlagCountry} is the ISO 3166
code the format wants: a country the converted InterCatch files name (\code{"Belgium"},
\code{"UK(Scotland)"}) is written as its code (\code{BE}, \code{GB-SCT}), and one with no code is
warned about and kept.
}

\subsection{The CAS}{

One row for each donor discard stratum of each group: \code{rate}, the discards over the
landings of the donor (the discard ratio, which can exceed 1), and \code{weightingTotal},
the landings that weight it. This is how \code{\link[=catchRaising]{catchRaising()}} combines them: the ratio of a
group is the mean of the donors' ratios weighted by their landings -
\code{averagingMethod} \code{"Weighted"}, \code{weightingCategory} \code{"Lan"} and \code{weightingParameter}
the variable of the raising (\code{"WeightLive"}) - and so \code{sum(rate * weightingTotal) / sum(weightingTotal)} of a group is the ratio the raised discards of the group were made
with. That is checked: a group whose donors do not give the ratio its raised discards
have is warned about - the conditions are not those of the raising, or the donors are
not all in the catch given. The CAS strata are rows of the CAR (\code{imported = "Y"},
\code{Dis}, with the group in its source), by the country, year, season, area and fleet.
}

\subsection{The header}{

\code{workingGroupYear}, \code{version}, \code{versionDescription}, \code{calendarYear} and
\code{startDateYear} are those of \code{\link[=catchCombined]{catchCombined()}} - give them the same values - and are
written on every row. \code{catchAllocationSchemeName} is the name of the scheme the discards
were allocated by; it is the \code{versionDescription} when not given.
}
